# The compile-fail suite byte-compares roughly 157 `.stderr` snapshots against
# what rustc prints. A checkout that rewrote them to CRLF would fail every one
# of them for a reason no contributor could act on, so line endings are
# normalized in the repository and checked out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Everything vendored is exempt, and this line has to come after the wildcard
# to win. `references/SHA256SUMS` pins the digest of each file and
# `mise run references:verify` checks it, so a filter that touched one byte on
# checkout would fail that gate -- and the point of vendoring a specification is
# that it is the bytes the standards body published, not a normalized copy.
references/** -text

references/rfc9110.txt -text whitespace=-trailing-space
